<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06WY">Variant <span data-tag="06WY">9.6.8.6</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer, let $S_{L}$ denote the collection of all categorically $n$-connective functors of $\infty $-categories (Definition <a data-tag="05BZ" href="/tag/05BZ">4.8.5.1</a>), and let $S_{R}$ denote the collection of all $n$-faithful functors of $\infty $-categories (Definition <a data-tag="05AX" href="/tag/05AX">4.8.3.12</a>). Then the pair $(S_ L, S_ R)$ is a factorization system on the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$. See Variant <a data-tag="06W8" href="/tag/06W8">9.6.6.7</a> and Theorem <a data-tag="05CS" href="/tag/05CS">4.8.7.3</a>. </p>
</article>
